    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1019,
      "versionNonce": 352524530,
      "index": "b3F",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "SLvjfNM7evRatO7H6zpbJ",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": -2716.0335307345185,
      "y": 868.274864709803,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 760.380859375,
      "height": 414,
      "seed": 100461170,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1714744626805,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "text": "1) declare and initialize a Set to any given available vertex. Let's say 0, so Set A = {0}.\n    Note that you have freedom to start at any vertex, not only 0.\n\n2) initialize smallestCosts (an array containing the costs of your path from your\nchosen vertex v to w). Copy the entire row. Let's say your chosen vertex as starting\npoint is 0, then copy all costs from 0-1, 0-2, 0-3, ... 0-4. We start initializing at i = 1.\n\n3) for ( x = 1 ; x < MAX ; x++){\n    a) choose a vertex HEAD in universal-visited (difference)\n    such that D[HEAD] is a minimum.\n    \n    b) add HEAD to visited\n\n    c) for each vertex PATH in universal-visited do\n                           \n    D[PATH] = min(D[PATH],      D[HEAD] + C[HEAD][PATH]);\n}\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) declare and initialize a Set to any given available vertex. Let's say 0, so Set A = {0}.\n    Note that you have freedom to start at any vertex, not only 0.\n\n2) initialize smallestCosts (an array containing the costs of your path from your\nchosen vertex v to w). Copy the entire row. Let's say your chosen vertex as starting\npoint is 0, then copy all costs from 0-1, 0-2, 0-3, ... 0-4. We start initializing at i = 1.\n\n3) for ( x = 1 ; x < MAX ; x++){\n    a) choose a vertex HEAD in universal-visited (difference)\n    such that D[HEAD] is a minimum.\n    \n    b) add HEAD to visited\n\n    c) for each vertex PATH in universal-visited do\n                           \n    D[PATH] = min(D[PATH],      D[HEAD] + C[HEAD][PATH]);\n}\n",
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
