      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "text": "Basically, the concept of Djikstra is that you declare and initialize an array of smallestCosts.\nIn each iteration and in each index of your smallestCosts, it will be constantly updated as\nnew paths will be visited with smaller costs. ",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Basically, the concept of Djikstra is that you declare and initialize an array of smallestCosts.\nIn each iteration and in each index of your smallestCosts, it will be constantly updated as\nnew paths will be visited with smaller costs. ",
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
